# Heretek-Crew ignores — fail-closed hygiene for secrets, dumps, workspace outputs.
# - .env / .env.local hold real secrets (see .env.example template). NEVER commit them.
# - backups/ holds pg_dump outputs (database bytes). NEVER commit them.
# - workspaces/ holds agent checkouts / runtime outputs; keep the dir, ignore contents.
# - Standard hygiene: logs, OS metadata, node_modules.

.env
.env.local
backups/
# ./secrets/ holds the read-only kubeconfig (KUBECONFIG_READONLY_PATH) and
# any other host-side credential files. NEVER commit cluster credentials.
secrets/*
!secrets/.gitkeep
workspaces/*
!workspaces/.gitkeep
# Wave D P2-7.2: the quarantined runner's dedicated /scratch bind source
# must exist host-owned before first `up` (else compose creates it
# root-owned and breaks the `node` runner). Only the placeholder is
# tracked — runner outputs written here at runtime stay ignored.
!workspaces/scratch/
workspaces/scratch/*
!workspaces/scratch/.gitkeep
.worktrees/*
!.worktrees/.gitkeep
*.log
references/

.DS_Store
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
